**Issue**: #1
**Date**: 2026-08-23
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: RussellBTech

Feature: Complete volunteer coverage coordination
  Volunteer Coordinator must let coordinators establish authoritative schedules and coverage
  while volunteers self-serve without persistent accounts.

  Scenario: Replace the legacy application
    Given remote master contains the tracked VSMS solution
    When issue #1 is delivered
    Then the legacy solution, projects, and obsolete artifacts are absent
    And the current lifecycle and steering contract is present
    And VolunteerCoordinator.sln and the six reserved projects are the only application layout
    And no legacy compatibility shim or data import is introduced

  Scenario: Coordinator starts from zero shifts
    Given the database contains no shifts
    And an allowlisted coordinator is authenticated
    When the coordinator opens schedule setup
    Then a textual empty state explains that shifts must be created
    And the coordinator can create the first shift

  Scenario: Coordinator manages and publishes a shift
    Given an allowlisted coordinator is authenticated
    And an active unpublished future shift exists
    When the coordinator edits its details and publishes it
    Then the corrected shift is persisted with one primary slot and its configured backup slots
    And the coordinator actions are audited

  Scenario: Volunteer discovers and requests an opening
    Given a published future shift has an unfilled slot
    When a volunteer browses openings and submits valid contact details
    Then one pending request is persisted
    And a private opaque status link is shown once
    And the opening and request states are expressed in text

  Scenario: Duplicate pending request is rejected
    Given a volunteer already has a pending request for a slot
    When the same volunteer requests that slot again
    Then no second pending request is created
    And a clear validation message is shown

  Scenario: Coordinator approves a request
    Given a pending request targets an open slot
    And an allowlisted coordinator is authenticated
    When the coordinator approves the request
    Then the volunteer receives the active assignment atomically
    And the request is approved
    And the action is audited

  Scenario: Coordinator rejects a request
    Given a pending request exists
    And an allowlisted coordinator is authenticated
    When the coordinator rejects the request
    Then the request is rejected without filling the slot
    And the action is audited

  Scenario: Coordinator reassigns a filled slot
    Given a slot has an active assignment
    And an allowlisted coordinator is authenticated
    When the coordinator reassigns the slot to another volunteer
    Then the previous assignment is marked reassigned
    And exactly one active assignment remains
    And the reassignment is audited

  Scenario: Volunteer confirms through a secure link
    Given an assignment is assigned
    And a valid unexpired unused confirm token exists for it
    When the volunteer posts the confirm action
    Then the token is consumed once
    And the assignment becomes confirmed
    And only the token hash remains persisted

  Scenario Outline: Invalid action link changes nothing
    Given an active assignment exists
    And the action token is <condition>
    When the volunteer attempts the action
    Then the assignment state is unchanged
    And the token is not accepted

    Examples:
      | condition  |
      | expired    |
      | already used |
      | bound to another assignment |
      | unknown    |

  Scenario: Volunteer declines an assignment
    Given an assigned volunteer has a valid decline link
    When the volunteer posts the decline action
    Then the assignment becomes declined
    And the slot becomes uncovered
    And the transition is audited

  Scenario: Volunteer cancels a confirmed assignment
    Given a confirmed volunteer has a valid cancel link
    When the volunteer posts the cancel action
    Then the assignment becomes cancelled
    And the slot becomes uncovered
    And the transition is audited

  Scenario: Coordinator monitors coverage
    Given published future shifts contain uncovered, assigned, and confirmed slots
    And an allowlisted coordinator is authenticated
    When the coordinator opens coverage monitoring
    Then uncovered slots are directly discoverable
    And unconfirmed assignments are directly discoverable
    And each state includes a text label
    And intervention actions are available

  Scenario: Notification failure remains separate
    Given a valid workflow transition is ready to commit
    And the notification adapter is unavailable
    When the transition completes
    Then authoritative workflow and audit state remain committed
    And notification failure is recorded separately

  Scenario: Non-allowlisted identity cannot coordinate
    Given an authenticated identity is absent from the coordinator allowlist
    When the identity requests a coordinator page
    Then access is forbidden

  Scenario: Public paths remain accountless
    Given no user is authenticated
    When a visitor opens shifts, submits a request, views status with a valid token, or uses a valid action token
    Then no coordinator login is required

  Scenario: Persistence uses PostgreSQL and UTC
    Given the application exercises persistence behavior
    When shifts and transitions are saved and loaded
    Then PostgreSQL stores every instant as UTC
    And no SQLite or EF in-memory persistence substitute is used
